<title>USA: Alcatel unit sues Corning/Siemens unit over patent.</title>
<headline>Alcatel unit sues Corning/Siemens unit over patent.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Del. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. subsidiary of Alcatel Alsthom has asked a federal court to rule that optical fiber cables made by Alcatel NA Cable Systems Inc do not infringe a patent owned by Siecor Corp.</p>
<p>In papers filed last week in the U.S. District Court in Delaware, Alcatel, the giant French telecommunications and engineering company, said it is &quot;resuming manufacture and sale of (its) products&quot; and alleges that Siecor's '352 patent for S-Z stranded optical cable is invalid and unenforceable.</p>
<p>Both Alcatel NA and Siecor, a joint venture of Corning Inc and Siemens AG, are based in Hickory, North Carolina.</p>
<p>A Siecor spokeswoman told Reuters no one at Siecor was available for comment at this time.</p>
</text>
